# Template only -- lists the variable names this stack's docker-compose.yml
# expects. Real values live in Infisical, never here and never in git.
# scripts/render-env.sh writes the actual .env next to this file on the host.
#

# --- Authentik OIDC login for YTzero ---
# YTzero is set up to authenticate via OIDC (YTZERO_AUTH_MODE=oidc is
# hardcoded in docker-compose.yml) against Authentik at auth.valdeze.ch,
# rather than having its own login system -- consistent with this repo's
# default of using Authentik OIDC for anything exposed externally.
#
# YTZERO_OIDC_ISSUER: the OIDC issuer URL for YTzero's application in
#   Authentik, typically something like
#   https://auth.valdeze.ch/application/o/<slug>/ .
# YTZERO_OIDC_CLIENT_ID / YTZERO_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET: the client
#   credentials for that same Authentik OIDC application/provider.
#
# YTzero itself is a genuinely unconfirmed stack per the homelab context
# brief's open questions -- what it actually does day to day, and how
# actively it's used/maintained, hasn't been nailed down. Treat the above
# as "how the compose file is wired," not as confirmation of how it's
# actually being used.
#
# Also note: there are no traefik.* labels anywhere in this stack's
# docker-compose.yml, even though YTZERO_BASE_URL points at
# https://yt.valdeze.ch (no internal/external.valdeze.ch split, and not
# even INTERNAL_DOMAIN-based) and it joins shared-services. It's unclear
# from this repo alone whether it's routed through Traefik's separate
# file-based (dynamic/) config, some other mechanism, or not routed yet --
# worth asking rather than assuming.
YTZERO_OIDC_ISSUER=REPLACE_ME
YTZERO_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=REPLACE_ME
YTZERO_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=REPLACE_ME
